Now I've understood the spec from the man page:
- When `treefiles = true`, the data is stored in a tree of files: `exportname/TREEXXXX/.../FILEXXXX`
- Files and directories are auto-created
- Files are deleted when the corresponding block becomes unused (this refers to TRIM)
- Block file size is fixed at 4096 bytes (TREEPAGESIZE)
- Each folder has at most 1024 files/subdirectories (TREEDIRSIZE)
- Nesting depth is calculated based on filesize
- filesize must be specified
- Mutually exclusive with multifile (treefiles takes precedence)

